schema: '0.4'
id: cytoscape_js-02-dense-stress-layout
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: cytoscape_js
category: network-and-graph-visualization
variant: dense-graph-stress-layout
prompt:
  context:
  - references/fim/overview/network-3d-graphics/cytoscape_js.md
  - references/fim/solution/cytoscape_js.md
  text: 'Build a Cytoscape.js dense-graph stress layout for a package dependency corpus

    with 2500 nodes and 9000 edges. Use fcose or cose-bilkent quality settings,

    label thresholds, edge opacity reduction, neighborhood-only edge emphasis, and

    a community filter to keep rendering readable. Include stress metrics for load

    time, layout duration, visible node count, hidden edge count, memory caution,

    and frames dropped during pan and zoom. Provide a fallback branch that switches

    to precomputed positions and disables animation when the graph exceeds the

    live-layout limit.

    '
  system: You generate artifacts for cytoscape_js. Output only the requested artifact content. No markdown fences, no explanations.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 6144
    temperature: 0.3
output:
  formats:
  - format: html
  - format: json
  renderer: cytoscape-js
  expected_artifact: Dense Cytoscape stress page plus machine-readable performance report.
  text_format: cytoscape_js
  artifact_kind: Dense Cytoscape stress page plus machine-readable performance report.
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - Uses Cytoscape layout extension settings appropriate for dense graphs.
  - 'Includes readability controls: label thresholds, filtering, and edge de-emphasis.'
  - Reports layout and interaction stress metrics.
  - Defines a precomputed-position fallback for excessive graph size.
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    description: YAML parses and declares both visualization and stress-report outputs.
    criteria: YAML parses and declares both visualization and stress-report outputs.
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    description: Covers dense data, layout, rendering limits, filtering, and fallback behavior.
    criteria: Covers dense data, layout, rendering limits, filtering, and fallback behavior.
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    description: Dense view remains interpretable through community and neighborhood focus.
    criteria: Dense view remains interpretable through community and neighborhood focus.
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    description: Handles large input without promising unlimited live layout performance.
    criteria: Handles large input without promising unlimited live layout performance.
  pass_conditions:
  - The prompt reflects Cytoscape's strengths and scale limits.
  - Stress metrics are visible and exported.
  - The dense graph has a clear fallback strategy.
tags:
- fim
- cytoscape-js
- dense-graph
- stress-layout
- fcose
- cose-bilkent
- performance
